FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: insert
Signature: void insert(node **root, int id, int at, int bt, int prior)
Description: /**
 * @brief Insert a new process node at the end of a linked list.
 *
 * Allocates memory for a new node, initializes its process data fields,
 * and appends it to the list. If the provided list is empty, the new
 * node becomes the head.
 *
 * @param root Pointer to the head pointer of the list. Modified to point
 *             to the new head if the list was empty.
 * @param id Process ID to assign to the new node.
 * @param at Arrival Time to assign to the new node.
 * @param bt Burst Time to assign to the new node.
 * @param prior Priority value to assign to the new node.
 *
 * @note Memory: Allocates a new `node` struct. The caller is responsible
 *       for freeing the entire list.
 * @note Error: The function does not signal errors. It assumes `malloc`
 *       succeeds; otherwise, the program may terminate.
 */
Dependencies: None

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION (REFERENCE ONLY - do NOT copy into test):
```c
// C program for the function called insert
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <assert.h>   /// for assert
#include <stdbool.h>  /// for boolean data type
#include <stdio.h>    /// for IO operations (`printf`)
#include <stdlib.h>  /// for memory allocation eg: `malloc`, `realloc`, `free`, `exit`

struct node {
     int ID;             ///< ID of the process node
     int AT;             ///< Arrival Time of the process node
     int BT;             ///< Burst Time of the process node
     int priority;       ///< Priority of the process node
     int CT;             ///< Completion Time of the process node
     int WT;             ///< Waiting Time of the process node
     int TAT;            ///< Turn Around Time of the process node
     struct node *next;  ///< pointer to the node
 };

// Target function implementation
void insert(node **root, int id, int at, int bt, int prior)
{
    // create a new node and initialize it
    node *new = (node *)malloc(sizeof(node));
    node *ptr = *root;
    new->ID = id;
    new->AT = at;
    new->BT = bt;
    new->priority = prior;
    new->next = NULL;
    new->CT = 0;
    new->WT = 0;
    new->TAT = 0;
    // if the root is null, make the new node the root
    if (*root == NULL)
    {
        *root = new;
        return;
    }
    // else traverse to the end of the queue and insert the new node there
    while (ptr->next != NULL)
    {
        ptr = ptr->next;
    }
    ptr->next = new;
    return;
}

```

